/*!
 * @defgroup linflexd_driver
 * @ingroup mod_communication LINFlexD Driver
 * @ingroup linflexd
 * @brief LINFlexD peripheral driver for LIN and UART communication.
 *
 * ## Key Features
 * - Dual-mode operation: LIN mode and UART mode on a shared hardware block
 * - Full LIN 2.1 / 2.2 / SAE J2602 protocol support
 * - UART mode with 7/8/15/16-bit word lengths and configurable parity
 * - Hardware checksum generation and verification
 * - Master and slave node support
 * - Hardware ID filters for automatic frame routing (LIN slave mode)
 * - Blocking, polling, and non-blocking (interrupt/DMA) transfer models
 * - Idle timeout detection (UART mode)
 * - Low-power sleep mode with automatic wakeup
 *
 * ## Architecture
 *
 * The LINFlexD driver is split into three layers:
 *
 * | Layer              | Files                                   | Visibility |
 * |--------------------|-----------------------------------------|------------|
 * | HW Access          | `linflexd_hw_access.h`                  | Internal   |
 * | UART Driver        | `linflexd_uart_driver.h / .c`           | Public     |
 * | LIN Driver         | `linflexd_lin_driver.h / .c`            | Public     |
 *
 * The HW access layer provides inline register accessors used by both
 * the UART and LIN driver layers. Application code should only use the
 * public driver APIs.
 *
 * ## Sub-modules
 * - @ref linflexd_uart — UART mode driver
 * - @ref linflexd_lin  — LIN mode driver
 *
 * ## Supported Standards
 * - LIN 2.0 / 2.1 / 2.2
 * - SAE J2602
 * - ISO 17987
 *
 * @note Only one mode (LIN or UART) can be active on a given LINFlexD
 *       instance at a time.
 */